>(3)
>How often does one get bags of holding without a wish? I tried to drag a
>Unicorn up to the level I last saw an altar and I got incredibly
>overstressed (Couldn't go up the stairs).  If I put on my ring of
>levitation, will I be able to get up it?

I usually can find BoH in the mines.  In the stores, look for bags.
Loot them.  If they bite you, they're bags of tricks.  If there's 
stuff in them, take it out, then pick up the bag.  If it costs > 10
(depending on your charisma) then it is almost assuredly holding
(although the blessed/cursed status is still open).  If it costs
< 10 it's a normal bag, #Name it (not individually, the whole class
of bags) "normal" or somesuch, and whenever you come across another
one, if it says 'normal' it aint a BoH.

As for the levitation, I think you can always go up when you're
floatin', but don't quote me on that.

>(4)
>What good is a Unicorn horn? (Is it better than my blessed +5 long
>sword?)

The *blessed* Unicorn Horn is one of the handiest items to have.  When
I get holy water (which is usually not until after the mines) the
first two things I bless are (a) my unicorn horn and (b) my luckstone
-- in that order (even if I have 2 cursed magic lamps! true!)  When a
blessed unicorn horn is a)pplied, it will cure nausea, sickness, halluc,
stun, conf, blindness, and restore ability.  It always works (although 
if you've lost multiple points, you may have to apply it several times,
to get a complete restoration of your stats.) whereas an uncursed horn
will only work about half the time, and a cursed horn will *cause* 
confusion, etc.  Also, if you dip them in bad potion (sickness, poison,
confusion) the potions become water.  This is also a way to ID these
unfriendly brews (as well as manufacture H2O)

